cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CORread, please cite it as below, together with the work it builds on (see references)."
title: "CORread: training CORnet models of the ventral visual stream to read"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kubala
    given-names: Vojtěch
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/vk4444/CORread"
url: "https://vk4444.github.io/CORread"
abstract: >-
  CORread is a Python library for training CORnet models of the primate ventral visual stream to read,
  after Hannagan et al. (2021). It generates byte-reproducible word stimuli, trains pre-literate,
  illiterate and literate CORnet-Z and CORnet-S networks with full provenance, measures the word
  selectivity of their dense-layer units, and lesions word-selective units to study the recovery of reading.
keywords:
  - CORnet
  - reading
  - visual word form area
  - neuronal recycling
  - computational neuroscience
  - deep learning
